  "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $A$ to the line $\\overset{\u27f7}{BC},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{\u27f7}{BC}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/26bb0e4cf177eec77164b76cb3b72986977ebe439fe39220ac820d7d3cc2a03b.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $A$ to $\\overset{\u27f7}{BC}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/decfd00e92564ee5b585db65f9c0e7939c870f25d6abe8127caf68744a9bab71.png)",
